From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 16:46:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wordcraft-aros: measure the event loop (WORDCRAFT_PERF),
 --window

Problem: the editor feels slow on x86_64 ABIv11 under QEMU TCG, and the
  cause is not known: input handling, logic and layout, page rendering,
  the GUI rasterizer, the blit and the loop's wake-ups are all candidates.
Rationale: with WORDCRAFT_PERF=<file>, every pass of the loop records its
  time asleep, input translation, app.logic, app.ui, tessellation, texture
  upload, rasterization and blit, the events it handled, the latency of
  its oldest and youngest event (IntuiMessage Seconds/Micros to the end of
  the blit, both GetSysTime through CurrentTime), page renders and their
  time (counters added to wordcraft-render::render_page), uploaded texture
  pixels and vertices. Records stay in memory and are written as CSV at
  exit. F9 is taken as a scenario marker. --window <w>x<h> sets the inner
  size so two sizes can be compared.
Scope: diagnostic. Without WORDCRAFT_PERF the loop only reads Instant a
  few times per frame; F9 reaches the app as before. wordcraft-render
  gains two relaxed atomic counters (not on wasm32).
Upstream-status: local-only.
Verification: see the port's evidence reports.
Removal: when the responsiveness work no longer needs it.
